{"name":"Kenya","hex":"#cca179","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Kenya","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A country in East Africa. Official name: Republic of Kenya."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Kenya"}],"entries":[{"title":"Kenya","blocks":[{"text":"Kenya, officially the Republic of Kenya, is a country located in East Africa. With an estimated population of more than 54.2 million as of mid-2026, it is the 26th-most populous country in the world and the seventh-most populous in Africa. Kenya's capital and largest city is Nairobi. The second-largest and oldest city is Mombasa, a port city located on Mombasa Island. Other major cities within the country include Kisumu, Nakuru and Eldoret. Going clockwise, Kenya is bordered by South Sudan to the northwest, Ethiopia to the north, Somalia to the east, the Indian Ocean to the southeast, Tanzania to the southwest, and Lake Victoria and Uganda to the west. Its geography, climate and population vary. In western Rift Valley counties, the landscape includes cold, snow-capped mountaintops with surrounding forests, wildlife, and fertile agricultural regions in temperate climates. In other areas there are dry, arid, and semi-arid climates, as well as absolute deserts."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Flag_of_Kenya.svg/330px-Flag_of_Kenya.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kenya","wikidata":"Q114"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Turkana_Boy.jpg/500px-Turkana_Boy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Turkana_Boy.jpg/500px-Turkana_Boy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Turkana boy, a 1.6-million-year-old Homo erectus fossil","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATurkana_Boy.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Lamu_door.jpg/500px-Lamu_door.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Lamu_door.jpg/1280px-Lamu_door.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Lamu_door.jpg/500px-Lamu_door.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A traditional Swahili carved wooden door in Lamu","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALamu_door.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Braun_Mombasa_UBHD.jpg/500px-Braun_Mombasa_UBHD.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Braun_Mombasa_UBHD.jpg/500px-Braun_Mombasa_UBHD.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Portuguese presence in Kenya lasted from 1498 until 1730. Mombasa was under Portuguese rule from 1593 to 1698 and again from 1728 to 1729.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABraun_Mombasa_UBHD.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Sculpture_of_Koitalel_Arap_Samoei.jpg/500px-Sculpture_of_Koitalel_Arap_Samoei.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Sculpture_of_Koitalel_Arap_Samoei.jpg/1280px-Sculpture_of_Koitalel_Arap_Samoei.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Sculpture_of_Koitalel_Arap_Samoei.jpg/500px-Sculpture_of_Koitalel_Arap_Samoei.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sculpture of Koitalel Arap Samoei in the Kenya National Library Service building","li